#
# target/linux/hisilicon/luofu/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
#
# STATUS: SCHEMATIC / UNTESTED / NOT A WORKING TARGET.
#
# Mapping: <openwrt>/target/linux/hisilicon/luofu/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
# (mode 0755). The board.d helper names and the sourcing layout differ between
# OpenWrt releases; this file follows the board_config_update/board_config_flush
# shape and must be checked against the release being targeted.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT FINAL, IN ONE FACT:
#   the wired path is gmac -> internal LSW switch -> PHY -> RJ45, and the LSW
#   switch has NO driver in any tree (TARGET-DESIGN.md 8.1). Until the switch
#   driver and its port model exist there is no correct LAN/WAN interface
#   assignment to write here. Do not hardcode the bench unit's cable port as a
#   board-wide fact: the only measured fact is that on the bench unit the
#   carrier-carrying GMII port is 0x14480000, behind the vendor switch
#   (TARGET-DESIGN.md 6.2; ETHERNET-BRINGUP-FRAMING.md 2).
#
# TODO(switch, TARGET-DESIGN.md 8.1):
#   - decide DSA vs switchdev and model the internal switch's ports;
#   - then replace the placeholder below with the real port map, e.g.
#       ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "<lan ifaces>" "<wan iface>"
#     plus any ucidef_set_interface_* for the model;
#   - confirm every port role from the board schematic, not from the vendor
#     overlay.
# TODO(board name): the root compatible of the draft DTS is
# "hisilicon,luofu-r116"; the image recipe sketch uses "cudy,wr3000-v2".
# sysupgrade's board match and this case statement must agree. The final
# compatible order is an open question (see README "Open questions").

. /lib/functions/board.sh
. /lib/functions/uci-defaults.sh

board_config_update

case "$(board_name)" in
hisilicon,luofu-r116|cudy,wr3000-v2)
	# PLACEHOLDER. No interface is configured on purpose: inventing one here
	# would produce a netifd config for a device that does not exist.
	:
	;;
*)
	echo "Unsupported board: $(board_name)" >&2
	exit 1
	;;
esac

board_config_flush

exit 0
